@* Key lost (docs/07). Phase 0 stub: the text only. Phase 3 ports AuthLayout and adds Restore and Start with no notes. *@

<main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-md px-4 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-xl font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Your notes cannot be opened</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
        Falcon Notes keeps your notes encrypted with a key stored by @PlatformName. That key is no longer available on
        this device, so the notes saved here cannot be read. This can happen after reinstalling the app or resetting the
        device's secure storage.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-stone-500">Nothing has been deleted. The unreadable data is kept aside in case the key comes back.</p>
</main>

@code {
    private static string PlatformName =>
        OperatingSystem.IsAndroid() ? "Android" : OperatingSystem.IsWindows() ? "Windows" : "macOS";
}
